00:01:10.541 --> 00:01:14.268
(inspirational music)

00:01:14.268 --> 00:01:16.643
- This could be the
greatest time you ever live

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:18.322
if you control what you focus on,

00:01:18.322 --> 00:01:20.025
if you find a more empowering meaning,

00:01:20.025 --> 00:01:22.314
and if you decide to
model the actions of those

00:01:22.314 --> 00:01:23.899
who succeeded before you.

00:01:23.899 --> 00:01:25.314
It can be the best financial time,

00:01:25.314 --> 00:01:26.241
the best emotional time,

00:01:26.241 --> 00:01:27.597
the best spiritual time of your life,

00:01:27.597 --> 00:01:29.323
but you better take control of your state.

00:01:29.323 --> 00:01:31.500
So, if you want to change
your life, my friends,

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:33.207
you've got to change your physiology

00:01:33.207 --> 00:01:35.493
and you got to change your focus.

00:01:35.493 --> 00:01:37.657
By the way, how fast can
you change that stuff?

00:01:37.657 --> 00:01:38.510
How fast, my friends?

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:39.343
How fast?

00:01:39.343 --> 00:01:40.863
How fast? Come on.

00:01:40.863 --> 00:01:43.813
In a heartbeat, once your
re-change your conditioning.

00:01:43.813 --> 00:01:45.721
That's all you got to do,

00:01:45.721 --> 00:01:47.071
and you can do it fast.

00:01:47.071 --> 00:01:48.584
You can do it a question or two.

00:01:48.584 --> 00:01:49.886
Try this right now.

00:01:49.886 --> 00:01:52.196
Answer this question in
your mind, and be honest.

00:01:52.196 --> 00:01:54.893
What, in your life today,
if you wanted to be,

00:01:54.893 --> 00:01:57.984
could you feel proud about right now?

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:59.173
If you wanted to feel proud.

00:01:59.173 --> 00:02:01.428
If you feel like I shouldn't be proud.

00:02:01.428 --> 00:02:03.122
If you wanted to feel proud,

00:02:03.122 --> 00:02:06.381
what could you be proud
of in your life today?

00:02:06.381 --> 00:02:08.361
Your children, your health, your body?

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:10.114
Is there a problem you faced,

00:02:10.114 --> 00:02:11.272
and instead of running from it,

00:02:11.272 --> 00:02:14.676
you finally stepped up and handled it?

00:02:14.676 --> 00:02:17.384
What could you feel proud
of in your life today,

00:02:17.384 --> 00:02:19.717
if you wanted to feel proud?

00:02:20.889 --> 00:02:23.114
How many could think of something?

00:02:23.114 --> 00:02:25.979
And when you think about
this thing you're proud of,

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:28.095
what about that makes you feel proud?

00:02:28.095 --> 00:02:32.068
What do you focus on that
makes you feel proud?

00:02:32.068 --> 00:02:35.544
How do you breathe when you
really start to feel proud?

00:02:35.544 --> 00:02:37.769
What's the kind of look on
your face that starts to happen

00:02:37.769 --> 00:02:40.433
when you let yourself feel proud?

00:02:40.433 --> 00:02:42.520
Yeah, how's that feel?

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:43.527
Think of another area of life.

00:02:43.527 --> 00:02:47.192
Think of an area of life
that you're grateful for,

00:02:47.192 --> 00:02:49.245
or if you go I'm not grateful,

00:02:49.245 --> 00:02:50.386
if you wanted to be grateful,

00:02:50.386 --> 00:02:54.375
what's an area you
could feel grateful for?

00:02:54.375 --> 00:02:55.310
What could you feel grateful for,

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:57.211
if you really wanted to feel grateful?

00:02:57.211 --> 00:02:59.607
If you wanted to be excited
about your life right now,

00:02:59.607 --> 00:03:00.717
and you were willing to be excited,

00:03:00.717 --> 00:03:02.563
you were willing to buck
everybody else's trend,

00:03:02.563 --> 00:03:04.649
what could you feel
excited about in your life

00:03:04.649 --> 00:03:06.037
if you wanted to feel excited?

00:03:06.037 --> 00:03:09.281
What could you get excited about
if you really focused on it

00:03:09.281 --> 00:03:11.584
and you really took it in?

00:03:11.584 --> 00:03:12.786
And you weren't in a negative place?

00:03:12.786 --> 00:03:14.310
What could you get excited about,

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:16.456
if you wanted to be excited in your life?

00:03:16.456 --> 00:03:19.325
Or when you're really
excited, how do you feel?

00:03:19.325 --> 00:03:20.177
How do you speak?

00:03:20.177 --> 00:03:22.190
What's your life like?

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:23.452
By the way, when you're excited,

00:03:23.452 --> 00:03:26.182
does it tend to touch
other people, yes or no?

00:03:26.182 --> 00:03:27.015
Absolutely.

00:03:27.015 --> 00:03:28.664
By the way, do people have a tendency,

00:03:28.664 --> 00:03:29.958
but who feels different right now

00:03:29.958 --> 00:03:31.285
than just even a couple moments ago?

00:03:31.285 --> 00:03:32.870
Raise your hand, say I.

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:36.703
Why? Because focus is
controlled by questions.

00:03:37.672 --> 00:03:39.879
If you ask a different
question continuously,

00:03:39.879 --> 00:03:41.355
not once, continuously,

00:03:41.355 --> 00:03:43.262
you will get a different answer.

00:03:43.262 --> 00:03:46.523
If you ask a lousy question,
you get a lousy answer

00:03:46.523 --> 00:03:48.809
and a lousy state.

00:03:48.809 --> 00:03:51.518
Somebody said why does
this always happen to me?

00:03:51.518 --> 00:03:53.245
It doesn't always happen to you,

00:03:53.245 --> 00:03:55.074
but the brain's like a computer.

00:03:55.074 --> 00:03:57.555
Ask it a question, it'll have
to come up with an answer.

00:03:57.555 --> 00:04:00.694
'Cause you deserve it, you idiot.

00:04:00.694 --> 00:04:03.280
Someone will say how come
I can never lose weight?

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:04.621
You can lose weight,
but if you keep saying

00:04:04.621 --> 00:04:05.679
how come I can't ever lose weight,

00:04:05.679 --> 00:04:06.895
the brain's got to come with an answer,

00:04:06.895 --> 00:04:08.395
goes you're a pig.

00:04:09.624 --> 00:04:11.513
Lousy question create what?

00:04:11.513 --> 00:04:12.635
Lousy answers.

00:04:12.635 --> 00:04:14.957
Ask a better question,
get a better answer.

00:04:14.957 --> 00:04:16.542
Now, here's what I want you to get.

00:04:16.542 --> 00:04:18.357
I want you to get that
you can change your state,

00:04:18.357 --> 00:04:19.190
how fast, guys?

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:20.023
How fast?

00:04:20.023 --> 00:04:20.917
How fast?

00:04:20.917 --> 00:04:22.668
And if you get the habit of doing it,

00:04:22.668 --> 00:04:23.977
you'll have a different life.

00:04:23.977 --> 00:04:26.386
- I was in an advising
session with a student, right?

00:04:26.386 --> 00:04:28.293
Man, I wish you guys
could have been there.

00:04:28.293 --> 00:04:29.999
So, I'm sitting with the student, right?

00:04:29.999 --> 00:04:31.949
And I begin to pull out my paperwork,

00:04:31.949 --> 00:04:34.479
and I'm about to share
with her her math grade,

00:04:34.479 --> 00:04:36.369
but before I could even open up my mouth,

00:04:36.369 --> 00:04:38.180
you know what she said to me?

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:39.975
Don't even talk about it.

00:04:39.975 --> 00:04:42.782
That's right, she told
me, ET, the motivator,

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:44.902
don't even talk about it.

00:04:44.902 --> 00:04:46.683
What she was saying was look,

00:04:46.683 --> 00:04:48.481
I'm not trying to be disrespectful,

00:04:48.481 --> 00:04:50.675
but I already know I'm not
doing that well in math.

00:04:50.675 --> 00:04:52.552
My teacher has talked to me about it.

00:04:52.552 --> 00:04:54.759
I've got a tutor, and guess what?

00:04:54.759 --> 00:04:57.824
ET, the motivator, there's
no way you can help me

00:04:57.824 --> 00:04:59.895
with this situation, so she said to me

00:04:59.895 --> 00:05:01.525
let's not even talk about it,

00:05:01.525 --> 00:05:03.523
and I'm telling some of
you out there right now,

00:05:03.523 --> 00:05:06.002
the reason why you are in
the situation you're in,

00:05:06.002 --> 00:05:08.991
because you keep talking about negativity.

00:05:08.991 --> 00:05:10.332
You keep talking about stuff

00:05:10.332 --> 00:05:13.804
that you can't do anything
about, so principle number two,

00:05:13.804 --> 00:05:17.342
real short and real sweet,
don't even talk about it,

00:05:17.342 --> 00:05:18.487
and you know what?

00:05:18.487 --> 00:05:20.082
I'm going to throw a tip in with that.

00:05:20.082 --> 00:05:21.626
Not only don't talk about it,

00:05:21.626 --> 00:05:24.534
but there's some things you
should even listen to, alright?

00:05:24.534 --> 00:05:27.399
Negativity, the things that
people are coming to you with

00:05:27.399 --> 00:05:28.785
that you know you can't change.

00:05:28.785 --> 00:05:29.929
There's nothing you can do about it.

00:05:29.929 --> 00:05:31.696
Don't just not talk about it,

00:05:31.696 --> 00:05:33.007
don't listen to it.

00:05:33.007 --> 00:05:35.157
I want you to know that,
from wherever you are,

00:05:35.157 --> 00:05:38.100
wherever you are, you can get
to where you need to get to

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.938
from that spot, right?

00:05:39.938 --> 00:05:41.504
I want to share something with you.

00:05:41.504 --> 00:05:42.926
Most of you guys know I was homeless

00:05:42.926 --> 00:05:44.344
for two and a half years, right?

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:45.898
Homeless for two and a half years,

00:05:45.898 --> 00:05:47.223
and a high school dropout,

00:05:47.223 --> 00:05:48.891
but one day, I just made up in my mind

00:05:48.891 --> 00:05:51.049
that I was not going
to allow homelessness,

00:05:51.049 --> 00:05:53.726
I was not going to allow
being a high school dropout,

00:05:53.726 --> 00:05:56.948
I was not going to allow
that to define who I was,

00:05:56.948 --> 00:05:58.454
and so I said you know what, Eric?

00:05:58.454 --> 00:05:59.382
It's manageable.

00:05:59.382 --> 00:06:01.306
It's manageable, but what you got to do,

00:06:01.306 --> 00:06:04.611
man, some of you, you
live seven days at a time.

00:06:04.611 --> 00:06:07.615
You live 30 days at a time,
and I had to say to myself,

00:06:07.615 --> 00:06:10.310
Eric, you can do this, but you know what?

00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:13.141
You're going to have to
do this one day at a time.

00:06:13.141 --> 00:06:15.203
That's right, one day at a time,

00:06:15.203 --> 00:06:17.547
and so I started studying for my GED,

00:06:17.547 --> 00:06:20.994
one day at a time, and I went
from a high school dropout

00:06:20.994 --> 00:06:23.869
to a college graduate,
to getting my masters,

00:06:23.869 --> 00:06:25.639
and working on my PhD.

00:06:25.639 --> 00:06:28.260
I went from being homeless
to being a homeowner,

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:30.225
so I want you to know, you can do it,

00:06:30.225 --> 00:06:32.209
but you got to break it up in pieces.

00:06:32.209 --> 00:06:35.026
That's right, take your
rent one month at a time.

00:06:35.026 --> 00:06:37.399
Take your life one day at a time,

00:06:37.399 --> 00:06:39.902
and I guarantee, if you
take it one day at a time,

00:06:39.902 --> 00:06:42.032
you will see how manageable it is,

00:06:42.032 --> 00:06:44.765
and one day you will look
up and you can get up.

00:06:44.765 --> 00:06:47.466
- I was a garbage man, like Troy.

00:06:47.466 --> 00:06:49.074
You get eight hours worth of work,

00:06:49.074 --> 00:06:50.677
but you can do it in three,

00:06:50.677 --> 00:06:52.749
so you can go home as soon as you finish.

00:06:52.749 --> 00:06:54.396
Post office, you get
three hours worth of work,

00:06:54.396 --> 00:06:56.329
and you make it last eight.

00:06:56.329 --> 00:06:58.041
I did both.

00:06:58.041 --> 00:07:00.507
I liked being the garbage man better,

00:07:00.507 --> 00:07:02.685
but they weren't bad jobs.

00:07:02.685 --> 00:07:04.509
It's like when people
say oh, the difficulty

00:07:04.509 --> 00:07:05.380
of making a movie.

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:06.769
I'm like send your son to Iraq.

00:07:06.769 --> 00:07:07.696
That's difficult.

00:07:07.696 --> 00:07:08.901
It's just a movie.

00:07:08.901 --> 00:07:11.612
It's like, relax, I don't
play that precious nonsense.

00:07:11.612 --> 00:07:13.812
Oh, a movie, oh, get out of here.

00:07:13.812 --> 00:07:15.099
You know?

00:07:15.099 --> 00:07:16.199
Your son got shot in the face?

00:07:16.199 --> 00:07:17.161
That's difficult.

00:07:17.161 --> 00:07:19.277
Making a movie is a luxury.

00:07:19.277 --> 00:07:20.727
It's a gift.

00:07:20.727 --> 00:07:23.209
It's an opportunity, and most
importantly, it's a gift.

00:07:23.209 --> 00:07:25.999
Obviously, everybody here is
talented enough to do that,

00:07:25.999 --> 00:07:27.413
but don't get it twisted.

00:07:27.413 --> 00:07:28.437
It's just a movie.

00:07:28.437 --> 00:07:29.626
It ain't that big a deal.

00:07:29.626 --> 00:07:31.363
- In the dark times, it's the easiest time

00:07:31.363 --> 00:07:33.557
to curl up in a ball, and
sometimes that's okay.

00:07:33.557 --> 00:07:34.777
If you need to have a bad day

00:07:34.777 --> 00:07:36.649
and sit on the couch and
watch a bunch of movies

00:07:36.649 --> 00:07:38.952
with some tissues, and
just go through a bad day

00:07:38.952 --> 00:07:41.494
and a few bags of potato chips, you know?

00:07:41.494 --> 00:07:43.811
A lot of people have to
deal with that situation,

00:07:43.811 --> 00:07:44.644
and it's okay,

00:07:44.644 --> 00:07:46.462
but if that happens day after
day after day after day,

00:07:46.462 --> 00:07:50.458
that's the time to take
control of your life back,

00:07:50.458 --> 00:07:52.655
or ask for some help, you know?

00:07:52.655 --> 00:07:56.452
Part of perspective isn't
just understanding our life

00:07:56.452 --> 00:07:59.134
has been better, understanding
that we have strengths

00:07:59.134 --> 00:08:00.274
and choice and will.

00:08:00.274 --> 00:08:03.477
It's understanding that
we aren't the only thing.

00:08:03.477 --> 00:08:06.278
That perspective reminds
us there's other people

00:08:06.278 --> 00:08:08.580
out in the world who we might
be able to connect with.

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:09.569
who can help us.

00:08:09.569 --> 00:08:11.629
To raise our hand and
connect with a friend

00:08:11.629 --> 00:08:14.707
or take somebody out for
lunch or to call a therapist

00:08:14.707 --> 00:08:17.067
or to get some support from other people,

00:08:17.067 --> 00:08:19.306
other family, other
friends, it's important.

00:08:19.306 --> 00:08:21.598
That's part of perspective as well.

00:08:21.598 --> 00:08:24.334
I would say, you know,
what else comes to mind

00:08:24.334 --> 00:08:26.943
when there's a difficult time is to ask

00:08:26.943 --> 00:08:30.019
what should I be learning here,

00:08:30.019 --> 00:08:32.698
because sometimes, when it's
really difficult in life,

00:08:32.698 --> 00:08:34.347
we don't feel competent.

00:08:34.347 --> 00:08:35.674
We don't feel capable.

00:08:35.674 --> 00:08:39.070
We feel like, you know, we
don't have any personal power.

00:08:39.070 --> 00:08:41.844
We don't have any knowledge of
how to proceed through there,

00:08:41.844 --> 00:08:44.086
so I tell people, when
you're in a difficult time,

00:08:44.086 --> 00:08:45.988
create like a learning map.

00:08:45.988 --> 00:08:48.228
You know, like okay, based on everything

00:08:48.228 --> 00:08:50.425
that's going on right
now, what are three things

00:08:50.425 --> 00:08:52.402
I need to start learning right now?

00:08:52.402 --> 00:08:54.126
You know, what can I
learn from this situation?

00:08:54.126 --> 00:08:55.467
That's always powerful, right?

00:08:55.467 --> 00:08:57.037
That's one powerful way to learn.

00:08:57.037 --> 00:08:58.410
Well, what can I learn from here?

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:00.878
What's the universe sending
a message to me right now?

00:09:00.878 --> 00:09:02.524
What can I learn from this situation,

00:09:02.524 --> 00:09:04.871
from my behavior or my beliefs?

00:09:04.871 --> 00:09:06.486
From my interactions with other people?

00:09:06.486 --> 00:09:08.193
But also, going to that next step

00:09:08.193 --> 00:09:10.002
and saying okay, at this point,

00:09:10.002 --> 00:09:12.713
what should I start learning in my life?

00:09:12.713 --> 00:09:14.776
And I know it sounds so weird, you know?

00:09:14.776 --> 00:09:17.543
I'm not saying hey, you know,
you're really depressed.

00:09:17.543 --> 00:09:19.263
It's time to start learning French.

00:09:19.263 --> 00:09:20.096
But you know what?

00:09:20.096 --> 00:09:22.863
It might help you, because in the process

00:09:22.863 --> 00:09:26.197
of learning something, our
brain starts activating

00:09:26.197 --> 00:09:28.697
in different ways that
also end up activating

00:09:28.697 --> 00:09:32.280
other parts of our brain's
capabilities to grow,

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:34.421
to cope, to deal.

00:09:34.421 --> 00:09:36.638
A great time to start learning again

00:09:36.638 --> 00:09:38.711
is the times when you feel just beaten up

00:09:38.711 --> 00:09:40.338
and kicked by the side of the road.

00:09:40.338 --> 00:09:41.755
It's time to stand up and say okay,

00:09:41.755 --> 00:09:44.362
what would I need to learn
now to advance my life

00:09:44.362 --> 00:09:46.146
to the next stage?

00:09:46.146 --> 00:09:47.636
Because look, no matter where you're at,

00:09:47.636 --> 00:09:49.804
if you're in a difficult
place in life right now,

00:09:49.804 --> 00:09:52.377
realize you've been in the last stage,

00:09:52.377 --> 00:09:53.886
and now there's going to be a new stage,

00:09:53.886 --> 00:09:56.570
so what will you have to learn
or master in this new stage

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:58.747
to feel better about
yourself or about life,

00:09:58.747 --> 00:10:00.484
or get ahead a little bit more.

00:10:00.484 --> 00:10:01.803
Don't forget that.

00:10:01.803 --> 00:10:04.340
- The way I handle things,
even in the few rare days

00:10:04.340 --> 00:10:05.756
when I really struggle,

00:10:05.756 --> 00:10:08.303
I take a real step back and make pretend

00:10:08.303 --> 00:10:10.023
that somebody called me and told me that

00:10:10.023 --> 00:10:12.613
my mother or daughter were killed.

00:10:12.613 --> 00:10:15.583
And I know that's very
dark, and I apologize,

00:10:15.583 --> 00:10:17.211
but it's really what I do.

00:10:17.211 --> 00:10:19.671
I literally am able to, at my deepest,

00:10:19.671 --> 00:10:22.427
most struggling moment within business,

00:10:22.427 --> 00:10:24.667
take a step back and remind myself

00:10:24.667 --> 00:10:27.059
that I can make a
drillion dollars tomorrow

00:10:27.059 --> 00:10:28.309
on bitcoin, and

00:10:29.612 --> 00:10:32.819
if something bad happened to
the people I love the most,

00:10:32.819 --> 00:10:34.038
that it would mean nothing,

00:10:34.038 --> 00:10:38.441
and it very consistently
rewires me very quickly.

00:10:38.441 --> 00:10:40.895
I just put business in perspective.

00:10:40.895 --> 00:10:44.034
At the end of the day,
you know, it's money.

00:10:44.034 --> 00:10:46.094
For me, it's not really
money, it's my legacy,

00:10:46.094 --> 00:10:50.283
so I get hurt by it a little bit more, but

00:10:50.283 --> 00:10:52.813
yeah, I mean, you know,
I put it in perspective.

00:10:52.813 --> 00:10:54.330
It's money, and you know what?

00:10:54.330 --> 00:10:57.048
Up until I had a daughter,
even while I was married,

00:10:57.048 --> 00:10:59.882
up until when I had Misha four years ago,

00:10:59.882 --> 00:11:03.223
I secretly wanted to lose all my money.

00:11:03.223 --> 00:11:07.135
I had this weird, twisted, dark fantasy

00:11:07.135 --> 00:11:11.100
of losing everything just
to rise again like a phoenix

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:12.350
and remind you.

00:11:13.925 --> 00:11:15.455
- So, if we're going
to talk about the power

00:11:15.455 --> 00:11:17.880
of shifting your perspective,
I think, in general,

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:19.495
people focus on the wrong things.

00:11:19.495 --> 00:11:22.717
I think, in general, most
people focus on the small things

00:11:22.717 --> 00:11:24.341
in their life, in their business,

00:11:24.341 --> 00:11:25.620
the things that are most immediate things,

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:27.198
that are most in front of their face,

00:11:27.198 --> 00:11:29.017
and it makes us play small
on a consistent basis.

00:11:29.017 --> 00:11:31.446
One of the most effective
strategies that I've found

00:11:31.446 --> 00:11:34.947
to help overcome an immediate
situation of despair

00:11:34.947 --> 00:11:37.568
or anger, frustration, is to be grateful,

00:11:37.568 --> 00:11:41.116
'cause you can't be grateful
and upset at the same time.

00:11:41.116 --> 00:11:42.818
If you're truly grateful and appreciative

00:11:42.818 --> 00:11:44.621
of what's happening,
then you can't be upset

00:11:44.621 --> 00:11:46.023
at the same time, so as an example,

00:11:46.023 --> 00:11:49.423
last week, I'm at my condo and
I'm waiting for the elevator,

00:11:49.423 --> 00:11:51.691
and it's just taking a really long time.

00:11:51.691 --> 00:11:52.775
I've got some heavy things.

00:11:52.775 --> 00:11:54.587
I can't take the stairs,
and so I'm waiting.

00:11:54.587 --> 00:11:56.750
Really frustrated that
the elevator hasn't come.

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:58.457
I think one of the
elevators is on service,

00:11:58.457 --> 00:11:59.950
and there must be a lot of
people going up and down.

00:11:59.950 --> 00:12:01.534
It's like I'm sitting there,
waiting for the elevator.

00:12:01.534 --> 00:12:03.015
I'm like when is the
elevator going to come?

00:12:03.015 --> 00:12:04.786
How often have you been in that situation,

00:12:04.786 --> 00:12:06.559
where you're waiting for the elevator,

00:12:06.559 --> 00:12:07.639
you're stuck in traffic,
or somebody is late,

00:12:07.639 --> 00:12:08.940
or somebody has let you down?

00:12:08.940 --> 00:12:11.640
And instead, I quickly
shifted my perspective,

00:12:11.640 --> 00:12:14.444
and I asked myself how can I turn this

00:12:14.444 --> 00:12:15.828
into a moment of appreciation?

00:12:15.828 --> 00:12:18.284
How can I trade my
expectations for appreciation?

00:12:18.284 --> 00:12:20.652
And I just thought of listen,
we've got these elevators,

00:12:20.652 --> 00:12:24.044
these magical boxes that
can transport us up and down

00:12:24.044 --> 00:12:26.299
flights of stairs so that
I don't have to carry

00:12:26.299 --> 00:12:28.766
these heavy boxes, and
I have to wait, you know

00:12:28.766 --> 00:12:31.419
30 seconds more for that
elevator to come down.

00:12:31.419 --> 00:12:33.230
That immediately shifted my perspective

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:35.015
to focus on what I do have,

00:12:35.015 --> 00:12:37.558
what I'm grateful for, instead
of focusing on the problem

00:12:37.558 --> 00:12:39.800
that I had, which is not
really that big a problem.

00:12:39.800 --> 00:12:42.147
And I think we can, in
general, do that for our life.

00:12:42.147 --> 00:12:43.714
Look at what you're so upset about.

00:12:43.714 --> 00:12:46.213
Look at what's causing you
so much massive frustration?

00:12:46.213 --> 00:12:47.752
The fact that you're
even watching this video

00:12:47.752 --> 00:12:49.034
means that you are better off

00:12:49.034 --> 00:12:50.954
than 95% of the people in the world,

00:12:50.954 --> 00:12:53.484
where people can't even, you
know, give themselves food

00:12:53.484 --> 00:12:56.786
or have a stable job, have no,
you know, income coming in.

00:12:56.786 --> 00:12:57.974
They don't have an education.

00:12:57.974 --> 00:13:00.903
Most of the people in the
world, you are better off than.

00:13:00.903 --> 00:13:02.396
There are a lot of people
who have started businesses

00:13:02.396 --> 00:13:04.334
and had way more success
in what you've done,

00:13:04.334 --> 00:13:07.015
and they started with way fewer resources

00:13:07.015 --> 00:13:08.874
than what you currently have right now,

00:13:08.874 --> 00:13:10.525
and what do we do, as entrepreneurs?

00:13:10.525 --> 00:13:12.085
We tend to focus on what we don't have.

00:13:12.085 --> 00:13:13.503
We don't have the finances.

00:13:13.503 --> 00:13:14.617
We don't have the resources.

00:13:14.617 --> 00:13:15.698
We don't have the education.

00:13:15.698 --> 00:13:16.707
We don't have the mentorship.

00:13:16.707 --> 00:13:17.695
We don't have the connections.

00:13:17.695 --> 00:13:19.663
We don't have, we don't have,
we don't have, we don't have,

00:13:19.663 --> 00:13:22.772
and that just continues
that cycle of frustration

00:13:22.772 --> 00:13:25.789
and anger and resentment and depression,

00:13:25.789 --> 00:13:27.465
and we never get to where we need to go,

00:13:27.465 --> 00:13:29.354
where instead, if you
focus on figuring out

00:13:29.354 --> 00:13:31.366
what you can do with
what you already have,

00:13:31.366 --> 00:13:33.649
and that you already
have enough inside you

00:13:33.649 --> 00:13:34.962
to build something amazing,

00:13:34.962 --> 00:13:37.553
if you can remind yourself of
that when you get frustrated,

00:13:37.553 --> 00:13:39.303
then that can help get
you out of the hole.

00:13:39.303 --> 00:13:41.571
That shifting of perspective
can allow you to go off

00:13:41.571 --> 00:13:43.661
and do amazing things, where otherwise,

00:13:43.661 --> 00:13:45.354
your day was set off down a negative path,

00:13:45.354 --> 00:13:47.017
so I hope that helps.

